// type-assert matrix cell — type-switch/raw-absent.
// A type switch dispatches on the dynamic type of a MANAGED `@I` scrutinee: a single-target case narrows the `@`-binder to its concrete type, an interface case matches by satisfaction, a multi-target case keeps the scrutinee type, `default` catches the rest; a typed-nil box matches its OWN case (present true) while an unset box runs `default` (present false) — no `case nil` — across every mode.
